WEBVTT - HUD NSPIRE Compliance Briefing

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.000
If you own or manage properties with Section 8 or HUD vouchers,
the rules for your property inspections have completely changed.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:09.800
HUD has replaced legacy UPCS standards
with the strict new NSPIRE federal scoring protocol.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:17.000
Under the new rules, minor oversights like a missing GFCI outlet within 6 feet of water
or an unsealed smoke alarm trigger an automatic 24-hour repair order.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:24.300
Water heater pressure relief pipes, egress issues, and door hardware
now carry severe point deductions that can fail an entire property.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:29.800
And if those items are not cleared immediately,
HUD can freeze your monthly rental subsidy payments.

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:35.000
Most landlords fail simply because they didn't know
what the inspector was looking for before they arrived.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:39.900
The NSPIRE Compliance Kit gives you the exact room-by-room self-audit checklist
and the automated NSPIRE scoring model to walk your building in advance.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:45.000
Catch and fix simple maintenance defects before the inspection,
protect your inspection score, and keep your rental income completely safe.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:49.800
